# Test data

The `.html` fixtures in this directory are pruned snapshots of the live
CourtReserve "My Reservations" page (`app.courtreserve.com/Online/Bookings/List/7031`).

## How they were created

1. **Saved from live data.** Log in to CourtReserve in a real Chromium, open the
   bookings list, and use the browser's "Save page as..." to capture the page
   as an MHTML file (`.mhtml`). The raw captures live outside the repo in
   `../test-data/` and are several MB each.

2. **Prune to reduce size.** The scrapers only read the
   `[data-testid="booking-tabs"]` subtree, so each capture is cut down to just
   that `<div>` and everything inside it. The MHTML body is quoted-printable
   encoded; decode it, then slice from `<div data-testid="booking-tabs">`
   through its matching closing `</div>`. The result is wrapped in a minimal
   HTML shell:

   ```html
   <!DOCTYPE html>
   <html lang="en">
   <head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Booking List | powered by CourtReserve</title></head>
   <body>
   <div data-testid="booking-tabs">...subtree...</div>
   </body>
   </html>
   ```

   This shrinks each fixture from ~4.8 MB to a few KB. The markup inside the
   `<div>` is byte-for-byte as the site served it; only the surrounding CSS,
   images, and scripts are removed.

## Fixtures

- `one-booking-two-people.html` — one editable booking ("Edit Reservation").
- `no-booking.html` — no booking cards.
- `booking-by-other-people.html` — three bookings: one added by someone else
  ("Details" button, not editable) and two owned by the current user
  ("Edit Reservation" button).
- `adding-player/` — raw MHTML captures of the edit-reservation flow, kept for
  reverse-engineering the (unimplemented) add/remove-player methods.

## Caveats

Because the CSS is gone, the fixtures have no realistic layout. Assertions on
geometry (bounding boxes, scrolling, hover targets) will not match production;
only DOM structure and text are faithful.
